---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const updated = new Date("2026-05-26");
const dateFormat = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-AU", { dateStyle: "long" });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy -- Ben Schembri"
  description="What this site tracks, what it doesn't, and where the data lives."
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString()}
          >{dateFormat.format(updated)}</time
        >
      </p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This is my personal blog. I try to respect your privacy, and I don't
        collect much data.
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      I use <a href="https://plausible.io" rel="noopener">Plausible</a> to count
      visits. It records the page URL, referrer, country, device type, and
      browser — nothing that identifies you. No cookies. No cross-site tracking.
      No profile-building.
    </p>
    <p>
      My Plausible instance is self-hosted on infrastructure I run. The script
      and event endpoint are served first-party from this domain and proxied
      through to my server — no third-party requests leave your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>What I don't collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies of any kind</li>
      <li>No advertising or marketing trackers</li>
      <li>No third-party analytics (Google, Meta, etc.)</li>
      <li>No forms, comments, or logins — there's nothing to submit</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which keeps short-term access
      logs (IP address, request path, user agent) for abuse prevention and
      traffic shaping. I don't read those per-visitor and don't use them for
      analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests? <a href="/connect">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 8vh, 5rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .page-head {
    margin-block-end: 2.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-system-ui);
    font-size: var(--font-size-fluid--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-fluid-0);
    margin-block-start: 0.25rem;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block-start: 2.5em;
    margin-block-end: 0.5em;
  }

  p {
    margin-block-end: 1.25em;
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.25em;
  }

  li {
    margin-block-end: 0.4em;
  }

  code {
    padding: 0.125em 0.375em;
    background-color: color-mix(
      in oklch,
      var(--alt) 15%,
      var(--surface-reading)
    );
    color: var(--alt-strong);
    border-radius: 0.25em;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  /* Matches the homepage hero stagger so navigating between pages feels
     continuous. Time-based, so opacity:0 only applies when it will animate. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .page-head > * {
      opacity: 0;
      animation: rise 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.21, 0.6, 0.35, 1) both;
    }
    .page-head > :nth-child(1) {
      animation-delay: 0.1s;
    }
    .page-head > :nth-child(2) {
      animation-delay: 0.2s;
    }
    .page-head > :nth-child(3) {
      animation-delay: 0.32s;
    }
  }

  @keyframes rise {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(1.25rem);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
